$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure for the Kumada
Reaction A Schlenk tube was charged with 1 (2.8 mg, 0.005 mmol), THF (1.5
mL), and 2-chloroanisole (0.0718 g, 0.5 mmol). To the stirred solution
was added dropwise a solution of 4-MeC6H4MgBr in THF (1.5 mL, 0.5 M in
THF) at 30°C. Stirring was continued at 30°C for 24 h. The reaction was
ceased by addition of H2O (10 mL) and several drops of AcOH. The mixture
was extracted with EtOAc (3 × 10 mL) and the combined organic layers were
dried over anhyd Na2SO4. The Na2SO4 was removed by filtration and washed
with EtOAc. The resulting solution was concentrated by rotary
evaporation, and the residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel (eluent: PE). N,N-diethyl-4-(p-tolyl)benzamide 1H NMR: δ 1.17
(b, 3H, Et), 1.26 (b, 3H, Et), 2.40 (s, 3H, Me), 3.33 (b, 2H, Et), 3.56
(b, 2H, Et), 7.26 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H, C6H4), 7.43 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H,
C6H4), 7.50 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H, C6H4), 7.60 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H, C6H4).
13C NMR: δ 13.21, 14.37, 21.23, 39.42, 43.51, 126.97, 127.00, 127.07,
129.70, 135.93, 137.64, 142.08, 171.33.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Kumada reaction, yield depends on catalyst loading
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Amido pincer nickel catalyzed Kumada cross-coupling of aryl, heteroaryl,
and vinyl chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Xue-Qi; Wang, Zhong-Xia
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2013), 24(16), 2081-2084

