$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-(10-Undecen-1-yl)-2,2-bithiophene (22). A freshly prepared solution of
compound 21 (75.8 mmol) was added dropwise to a mixture of
2-bromothiophene (12.36 g, 75.8 mmol), Pd(dppf)Cl2 (278 mg, 0.4 mmol),
and 150 mL of anhydrous THF, while the temperature was kept between 0 and
10 °C. Then cooling was removed and stirring was continued for an
additional 2 h. Afterward it was poured into 300 mL of ice/water and
extracted twice with freshly distilled toluene. The organic phase was
separated, washed with water, and dried over sodium sulfate. The solvent
was removed by rotary evaporator to give 24.00 g of a crude product. The
product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel (eluent
hexane) to give pure compound 22 (21.61 g, 89%). Tm = 26 °C. 1H NMR (250
MHz, δ in CDCl3, TMS/ppm): 1.22-1.45 (overlapped peaks with a max. at
1.28, 12H, -CH2-CH2-CH2-), 1.67 (m, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz, -T-CH2-CH2-), 2.03
(m, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz, CH2═CH-CH2-), 2.77 (t, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz, -T-CH2-CH2-),
4.95 (m, 2H, CH2 d CH-CH2-), 5.80 (m, 1H, CH2═C H-CH2-), 6.67 (d, 1H, J =
3.7 Hz, thiophene-H), 6.98 (dd, 2H, J1 = 3.7 Hz, J2 = 4.9 Hz,
thiophene-H), 7.08 (dd, 1H, J1 = 3.7 Hz, J2 = 1.2 Hz, thiophene-H), 7.15
(dd, 1H, J1 = 4.9 Hz, J2 = 1.2 Hz, thiophene-H). 13C NMR (δ in CDCl3):
28.94, 29.07, 29.13, 29.35, 29.47, 29.49, 30.15, 31.61, 33.83, 114.12,
122.95, 123.35, 123.68, 124.68, 127.65, 134.73, 137.95, 139.23, 145.34.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Kumada coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Monochlorosilyl Derivatives of Dialkyloligothiophenes for
Self-Assembling Monolayer Field-Effect Transistors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ponomarenko, Sergei A.; Borshchev, Oleg V.; Meyer-Friedrichsen, Timo;
Pleshkova, Alexandra P.; Setayesh, Sepas; Smits, Edsger C. P.;
Mathijssen, Simon G. J.; de Leeuw, Dago M.; Kirchmeyer, Stephan;
Muzafarov, Aziz M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organometallics (2010), 29(19), 4213-4226

