$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the KCT reaction B. PICB-NHC-Ni catalyst 6b (29 mg
to 38 mg, 0.00026 mmol, 0.50 mol% as Ni) (loading of cat 6b is depending
of the lot: 0.086 mmol/g to 0.066 mmol/g) and LiBr (0.5 mmol, 1 equiv)
were placed in a a Schlenk tube-type and heated with a hair dryer in
vacuo for 2 minutes. Aryl or Vinyl or Alkyl halide (0.5 mmol, 1 equiv)
and Grignard reagents (0.63 mmol, 1.25 equiv) were introduced, and then
the solvent volume was adjusted with dried and degassed THF to a volume
of 0.75 mL. The mixture was for 12 h at room temperature. The reaction
was quenched by adding EtOH (0.5 mL). The catalyst was collected by
filtration using KIRIYAMAROHTO® funnel and washed with EtOAc. The
solution was hydrolyzed with saturated aqueous NH4Cl (10 mL) and the
aqueous phase was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic
phases were dried over MgSO4 and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The
residue was purified by TLC preparative. 1,3-dichlorobenzene (57 μL, 0.5
mmol, 1 equiv) and phenylmagnesium chloride (0.625 mL, 1.25 mmol, 2 M in
THF solution, 2.5 equiv) and LiBr (87 mg, 1 mmol, 2.0 equiv). The
reaction was heated at 65°C for 12h. The crude reaction mixture was
purified TLC preparative hexane (100) to provide 9fa. m-Terphenyl as
white solid, yield 102 mg, 88%. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3, 25°C): δ (ppm)
7.84 (t, J = 2 Hz, 1H), 7.68 (dt, J = 1.5 and 8.5 Hz, 4H), 7.61 (bd, J =
6 Hz, 2H), 7.54 (t, J = 7 Hz, 1H), 7.48 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 4H), 7.39 (t, J =
7 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3, 25°C): δ (ppm) 142.0,141.4, 129.4,
129.0, 127.6, 127.5, 126.4, 126.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst prepared and used, catalyst is a reaction product with a
bromoalkyl polystyrene, nickel, LiBEt3H, and DBU
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copolymer-Incarcerated Nickel Nanoparticles with N-Heterocyclic Carbene
Precursors as Active Cross-Linking Agents for Corriu-Kumada-Tamao
Reaction
