$DATUM 5-Ethyl-5'''-(5-undecenyl)-2,2':5',2'':5'',2'''-quaterthiophene (9). A
freshly prepared solution of compound 21 was added dropwise to a mixture
of compound 19 (7.15 g, 20 mmol), Pd(dppf)Cl2 (147 mg, 0.2 mmol), and 100
mL of anhydrous THF, while the temp- erature was kept between 0 and 10
°C. Then cooling was removed, and stirring was continued for an
additional 2 h. Afterward the mixture was poured into 200 mL of ice/water
and extracted twice with freshly distilled toluene. The organic phase was
separated, washed with water, and dried over sodium sulfate. The solvent
wasremoved by rotary evaporator to yield the crude product as a yellow
solid. The product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
(eluent toluene, 65 °C) followed by recrystallization from hexane/toluene
to give pure compound 9 as a yellow powder (9.07 g, 88%). Tm = 166 °C. 1H
NMR (250 MHz, δ in CDCl3, TMS/ppm): 1.21-1.47 (overlapped peaks with a
max. at 1.31, 15H, -CH2-CH2-CH2- including t at 1.33 ppm, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H,
-CH2-CH3), 1.68 (m, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz, -T-CH2-CH2-), 2.04 (m, 2H, J1 = 7.3
Hz, CH2═CH-CH2-), 2.80 (t, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz, -T-CH2-CH2-), 2.87(t,2H,
J=7.3Hz, -T-CH2-CH2-), 4.96 (m, 2H, CH2═CH-CH2-), 5.81 (m, 1H,
CH2═CH-CH2-), 6.68 (d, 1H, J = 3.7 Hz, thiophene-H), 6.72 (d, 1H, J = 3.7
Hz, thiophene-H), 6.98 (d, 2H, J = 3.7 Hz, thiophene-H), 7.01 (d, 2H, J =
3.7 Hz, thiophene-H), 7.05 (d, 2H, J = 3.7 Hz, thiophene-H).
