$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):AMD
$DATUM reaction products with a bromoalkyl polystyrene, nickel, LiBEt3H, and DBU
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the KCT reaction B.
PICB-NHC-Ni catalyst 6b (29 mg to 38 mg, 0.00026 mmol, 0.50 mol% as Ni)
(loading of cat 6b is depending of the lot: 0.086 mmol/g to 0.066 mmol/g)
and LiBr (0.5 mmol, 1 equiv) were placed in a a Schlenk tube-type and
heated with a hair dryer in vacuo for 2 minutes. Aryl or Vinyl or Alkyl
halide (0.5 mmol, 1 equiv) and Grignard reagents (0.63 mmol, 1.25 equiv)
were introduced, and then the solvent volume was adjusted with dried and
degassed THF to a volume of 0.75 mL. The mixture was for 12 h at room
temperature. The reaction was quenched by adding EtOH (0.5 mL). The
catalyst was collected by filtration using KIRIYAMAROHTO® funnel and
washed with EtOAc. The solution was hydrolyzed with saturated aqueous
NH4Cl (10 mL) and the aqueous phase was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 10 mL).
The combined organic phases were dried over MgSO4 and the solvent was
removed in vacuo. The residue was purified by TLC preparative.
1,3-dichlorobenzene (57 μL, 0.5 mmol, 1 equiv) and phenylmagnesium
chloride (0.625 mL, 1.25 mmol, 2 M in THF solution, 2.5 equiv) and LiBr
(87 mg, 1 mmol, 2.0 equiv). The reaction was heated at 65°C for 12h. The
crude reaction mixture was purified TLC preparative hexane (100) to
provide 9fa. 1-chloro-4-fluorobenzene (54 μL, 0.5 mmol, 1 equiv) and
tert-phenyl-phenylmagnesium bromide (1.26 mL, 1.26 mmol, 1 M in THF
solution, 2.5 equiv) and LiBr (87 mg, 1 mmol, 2.0 equiv). The reaction
was heated at 100°C in DME (0.75 mL) for 12h. The crude reaction mixture
was purified TLC preparative hexane (100).
1,4-bis(4-tert-Butylterphenyl)benzene as white solid, yield 252 mg, 85%.
1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3, 25°C): δ (ppm) 7.65 (s, 4H), 7.59 (d, J = 8 Hz,
4H), 7.48 (d, J = 8 Hz, 4H), 1.37 (s, 18H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3,
25°C): δ (ppm) 150.5, 139.9, 138.1, 127.5, 126.9, 126.0, 34.8, 31.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst prepared and used, catalyst is a reaction product with a
bromoalkyl polystyrene, nickel, LiBEt3H, and DBU
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copolymer-Incarcerated Nickel Nanoparticles with N-Heterocyclic Carbene
Precursors as Active Cross-Linking Agents for Corriu-Kumada-Tamao
Reaction
