$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Cross-Coupling
Reactions. A Schlenk tube was charged with 2.0 mg (4 μmol) of the desired
nickel complex and 3 mL of toluene or THF. The electrophilic coupling
partner (1.0 mmol) was then added, followed by the Grignard reagent (1.3
mmol) as a solution in THF. The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 6-12 h before being quenched with 5 mL of deionized
water. To the quenched reaction mixture was added 10 mL of diethyl ether,
causing separation of the organic layer. The organic layer was extracted
and dried over Na2SO4. After filtration and evaporation of the solvents
the crude product was purified by column chromatography on Al2O3 (3%
EtOAc in hexanes). Entry: 4; Yield 85%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
